{"id":"pwl_081","topic":"Progressive World Locking","subtask":"Branch-Aware Eviction Policy","description":"Ensure rolling window does not invalidate active branches. Eviction must consider snapshot graph, not just linear history.","subtasks":["Track snapshot graph: parent-child relationships.","When evicting, ensure snapshot has no active descendants.","If snapshot has children: either (A) prevent eviction, (B) rebase children, or (C) detach branch.","Provide policy selection: STRICT (no eviction if referenced), REBASE, FORCE.","Update branch metadata after eviction/rebase."],"verification":["Branches remain valid after eviction.","No orphaned snapshots.","Rebased branches produce correct world states."],"stress_test_conditions":["Deep branching (100 branches) with rolling window active.","Frequent commits on multiple branches."],"baseline_metrics":["Graph traversal <0.2ms for 1k snapshots."],"tooling_required":["Snapshot graph"],"action":"do_now","complexity_score":5}

{"id":"pwl_082","topic":"Progressive World Locking","subtask":"Undo/Redo Integration with Rolling Window","description":"Align undo/redo system with bounded snapshot history. Ensure undo stack respects eviction constraints.","subtasks":["Limit undo stack to max_snapshots.","When oldest snapshot evicted, remove corresponding undo entries.","Redo stack invalidated if snapshots fall outside window.","Provide user feedback when undo limit reached.","Optional: soft-warning before irreversible operations."],"verification":["Undo limited to available snapshots (e.g., 10 steps).","Redo behaves correctly within window.","No crashes when undo references evicted snapshot."],"stress_test_conditions":["Rapid undo/redo with continuous commits.","Undo at boundary (oldest snapshot)."],"baseline_metrics":["Undo latency unchanged (<5ms)."],"tooling_required":["Undo system"],"action":"do_now","complexity_score":3}

{"id":"pwl_083","topic":"Progressive World Locking","subtask":"Adaptive Window Scaling (User/Resource Driven)","description":"Allow dynamic adjustment of snapshot window size based on available memory or user preference.","subtasks":["Expose API: set_snapshot_window(N).","Monitor memory usage; if exceeding threshold, shrink window.","If memory available, optionally expand window (soft cap).","Persist user preference per project.","Integrate with GC and compaction."],"verification":["Window size changes at runtime without corruption.","Memory usage adapts accordingly.","Rollback range updates dynamically."],"stress_test_conditions":["Rapid scaling up/down of window size.","Memory pressure events."],"baseline_metrics":["Resize operation <1ms."],"tooling_required":["Memory tracker"],"action":"do_now","complexity_score":4}

{"id":"pwl_084","topic":"Progressive World Locking","subtask":"Temporal Feedback Loop (Learning Constraint)","description":"Enforce the '10-step learning loop' as an engine-level constraint: user must resolve changes within window or lose earliest states, shaping iterative behavior.","subtasks":["Expose optional mode: enforced_window_mode=true.","Display remaining rollback depth (e.g., '8/10 steps left').","Warn user when approaching eviction boundary.","Optional: prevent commit if unresolved conflicts exist near boundary.","Log user interaction patterns (how often they hit limit)."],"verification":["User sees decreasing rollback window.","Old states disappear as expected.","System encourages short iteration cycles."],"stress_test_conditions":["User commits rapidly without resolving changes.","Window boundary reached frequently."],"baseline_metrics":["UI update overhead negligible."],"tooling_required":["UI layer","Snapshot system"],"action":"do_now","complexity_score":3}

{"id":"pwl_085","topic":"Progressive World Locking","subtask":"Network Synchronization with Rolling Window","description":"Ensure multiplayer snapshot sync respects bounded history. Clients cannot request snapshots older than server window.","subtasks":["Server advertises snapshot window range [min_id, max_id].","Client requesting older snapshot → fallback to full snapshot sync.","Delta streaming limited to window range.","Handle desync: if client too far behind, resync fully.","Compress rolling window for network efficiency."],"verification":["Clients sync correctly within window.","Out-of-range requests handled gracefully.","Bandwidth remains bounded."],"stress_test_conditions":["Client joins late after many commits.","High latency causing client lag behind window."],"baseline_metrics":["Resync time <200ms.","Bandwidth stable."],"tooling_required":["Networking layer"],"action":"do_now","complexity_score":4}

{"id":"pwl_086","topic":"Progressive World Locking","subtask":"Dual-Layer Versioning (Local PWL + External VCS Bridge)","description":"Separate world evolution into two layers: (1) high-frequency local snapshot window (PWL), (2) low-frequency durable commits to external VCS (Git). The engine operates primarily on PWL, with periodic export to VCS.","subtasks":["Define VersionLayer enum: LOCAL_PWL, EXTERNAL_VCS.","Local commits (PWL) occur every interaction (high frequency).","External commits triggered manually or at milestones (low frequency).","Map snapshot_id → vcs_commit_id (optional link).","Provide API: export_snapshot_to_vcs(snapshot_id).","Do not require VCS presence for engine operation (offline-first)."],"verification":["Engine runs without VCS.","Export creates valid VCS commit.","Snapshots can be linked to commits."],"stress_test_conditions":["Thousands of local commits, few VCS commits.","Disconnected (offline) workflow."],"baseline_metrics":["Export overhead <200ms for medium project."],"tooling_required":["VFS","external process invocation"],"action":"do_now","complexity_score":4}

{"id":"pwl_087","topic":"Progressive World Locking","subtask":"Snapshot → File Projection (Deterministic Export)","description":"Convert a world snapshot into a deterministic file structure suitable for VCS storage. Ensures that world state can be versioned as files.","subtasks":["Serialize snapshot into directory structure: /entities/, /assets/, /scene.json.","Ensure stable ordering (canonicalization).","Split large blobs into chunked files (avoid large single files).","Compress assets selectively (not everything).","Generate manifest linking files to snapshot hash."],"verification":["Same snapshot → identical file output.","VCS diff shows meaningful changes.","Files reconstruct world state exactly."],"stress_test_conditions":["Large world (10k entities).","Cross-platform export consistency."],"baseline_metrics":["Export size < equivalent asset footprint.","Serialization <500ms."],"tooling_required":["Serializer","VFS"],"action":"do_now","complexity_score":5}

{"id":"pwl_088","topic":"Progressive World Locking","subtask":"Incremental VCS Export (Delta-Aware Commit)","description":"Only export changes between last exported snapshot and current snapshot to VCS, minimizing disk and network usage.","subtasks":["Track last_exported_snapshot_id.","Compute diff between snapshots (reuse pwl_057).","Export only modified entities/assets.","Update manifest incrementally.","Commit to VCS with message referencing snapshot metadata."],"verification":["Only changed files appear in VCS diff.","Export faster than full snapshot export.","No missing dependencies."],"stress_test_conditions":["Frequent exports (every few commits).","Large asset changes."],"baseline_metrics":["Export delta <10% of full snapshot size for small changes."],"tooling_required":["Diff system","VCS bridge"],"action":"do_now","complexity_score":4}

{"id":"pwl_089","topic":"Progressive World Locking","subtask":"Hardware-Aware Snapshot Tiering (RAM vs Disk vs Archive)","description":"Distribute snapshot storage across memory tiers: active window in RAM, extended history on disk, long-term archive via VCS.","subtasks":["Tier 1: RAM → rolling window (e.g., 10 snapshots).","Tier 2: Disk → extended snapshots beyond window (optional cache).","Tier 3: VCS → durable archive (exported snapshots).","Evicted RAM snapshots optionally spill to disk instead of deletion.","Lazy load disk snapshots when needed."],"verification":["RAM usage bounded.","Disk cache used when enabled.","Snapshots recoverable from disk or VCS."],"stress_test_conditions":["Low RAM system.","Large project (GB-scale assets)."],"baseline_metrics":["RAM usage constant.","Disk I/O <5ms per load (cached)."],"tooling_required":["VFS","GC"],"action":"do_now","complexity_score":5}

